From: EglantinePS5
Subject: [PATCH] up: EDEN_UP_PIPELINE_COUNT=1 (off unless set): a pipeline count line every 60 s

Idea: lethevimlet (oot-bc250 / lichii-bc250, branch mem/kept-pipelines, 1041d43eaf "vulkan: log the
built graphics pipeline count when it changes (every 600 frames)"); his note: on the BC-250 built
pipelines and the driver's data for them grew without bound over a long session. The upstream-news
ACT item (13 Nov) asks the same of ours: how many built pipelines over a long session, and how many
are built after launch in a warm run. The code is ours: his counts graphics pipelines in his cache
every 600 frames; this counts graphics, mesh and compute objects on a 60 s timer.

What (vk_pipeline_count.h, header only): every 60 s one line
  EDEN_UP_PIPELINE_COUNT: t=<s> s (60 s): graphics/mesh/compute alive a/b/c (total n), built ...,
  destroyed ..., warm (after preload) ...; preload ended at t=<s> s
plus one line when the boot preload ends and one at the rasterizer's end. Built = a GraphicsPipeline
or ComputePipeline whose driver pipeline was made (after MakePipeline / the compute driver call);
mesh = a GraphicsPipeline whose first stage is a task or mesh program, counted once also when its
programs run as compute. Destroyed = such an object's destructor while it holds its driver pipeline.
Warm = built after RasterizerVulkan::LoadDiskResources returned (the pipeline cache's preload and
its waits are over). t counts from the start of LoadDiskResources. Counts are relaxed atomics.

Off (unset): one cached flag load per pipeline build and per pipeline destructor; no thread, no
line. Behaves as T181.

KEEPS THE STORE: no id input touched. vk_pipeline_cache.cpp (rewritten into the id input
<build>/vk_pipeline_cache_cost.cpp) and vk_pipeline_cache.h are untouched; the edited files are
vk_graphics_pipeline.{h,cpp}, vk_compute_pipeline.{h,cpp}, vk_rasterizer.cpp and the new
vk_pipeline_count.h, none reached from src/shader_recompiler. No name added to TranslationSwitches.
